incident("GATE-GENERALIZE-G2G3") = {
  body: "Q2/Q3 closure: the package-conformance gate was vOSLAB-specific and two declared residuals (G2 P5-tautology, G3 registry-trust) were not yet action. Also the gate did not audit child/scripts (its own engine) and was not reusable for other projects. USER authorized resolving all Q2 points in parent and proceeding with (1) gate generalization + (2) a general discipline canon.",
  root_cause: "Discipline was declared-as-future (G2/G3 'action-ifiable at build time') rather than coded; the gate hardcoded registry('voslab') and did not enumerate child/scripts.",
  fix: "Gate now parameterized: check(root, child, registry_name='voslab') + parse_registry(text, registry_name); captures per-package status. G2 implemented as P5-SPECSRC-MISSING — a plan's source_spec must reference a RESOLVABLE spec file under root (exempt: 'build from scratch'). G3 implemented as P6-DANGLING-REGISTRY — only 'stable' registry packages must have a built artifact under ~/vOSlab/packages/*/<underscored-name> (design-status legitimately unbuilt; names normalized hyphen<->underscore). child/scripts now enumerated and mapped to gate-suite in the audit (found 3 previously-unmapped child scripts: hook_metrics.py, load_hooks.py, process_staging.py). Discipline distilled to child/docs/discipline/recursive_rigor.vsm (D1-D6, project-agnostic canon).",
  lesson: "A residual logged as 'future' is still declaration. Make it ACTION the moment authority exists; the gate caught a REAL defect (vsf-predicates source_spec had a trailing '.' -> 'scripts/vsl/classifier/*_predicates.py.' resolved to nothing) — G2 is not theoretical. Generalize discipline at write-time, not as migration cleanup.",
  references: ["scripts/vsl/check_package_conformance.py", "docs/discipline/recursive_rigor.vsm", "docs/vos_package_audit.vsm", "docs/vos_package_detailed_plans.vsm", "checks/package-conformance-valid"],
}
⟦ /gate_generalize_g2g3 ⟧
